## What to deliver

Build and rig the mech up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png` matches
the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together correctly,
and the rig is complete: an armored body and head standing on two legs with visibly
bent knees, a broad tower shield carried on a visible left arm, and a heavy siege maul
in a visible right arm. **Author the two required animations** as F-curves with the
`voxel-anim` animation subcommands: `walk` (a walk whose feet plant flat and still,
then lift and swing — with weight, not a weightless slide — the two legs in opposite
phase so one foot is always down) and `smash` (the maul winding up overhead and
slamming down while the mech stands still). The animations are the fixed contract —
produce both, by those names; the parts and joints that realize them are yours. When
you are satisfied, stop: the recorded per-part logs and `rig.json` are your finished
submission.
